From 34856e996cd1625180d383552fbde2162ad40593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:55:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip the SCTP tests that need lo0 aliases or IPv6 on
 Darwin

The gateway tests exercise multihoming and IPv6 by binding endpoints to
127.0.0.2 through 127.0.0.5 and to ::1. On macOS the SCTP stack behind
the socket API is usrsctp over UDP encapsulation (libsctp-compat). With
an endpoint bound to an lo0 alias the INIT handshake completes, but no
later packet is delivered to either side: data is lost and a shutdown
never completes, so a test waiting for SCTP_SHUTDOWN_COMP blocks the
whole binary. IPv6 SCTP is not used by this port and untested there.

Add OCUDU_SKIP_IF_NO_LO0_ALIAS_OR_IPV6_SCTP(), a GTEST_SKIP on Darwin
and a no-op elsewhere, and call it at the top of the affected tests: six
client tests, one server test, five socket tests and the eight
parameterised server peer tests whose fixture binds three servers to
aliases. Every test that stays on 127.0.0.1 keeps running.
